IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrca-member`
IMPORT `mrca-guide`
IMPORT `mrca-formulas`

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 -- worked cases for the amounts computed from the formulas sidecar
-- (C2004A01285.formulas.md), from the seat of the current or former member.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the formulas, the deposited text and the Guide's Table 23.1, never copied from the encoding's output; the working
-- is in the comment above each case. No scenario life raised this Act; every case is HYPOTHETICAL. The s 74 maximum of
-- $421.72 is the figure the Guide's own example uses; the Actuary's factors (900 at the person's age, 1,000 for a male
-- aged 30), the minimum wage ($24.95) and the CPI numbers are made-up figures.
--
-- Sam (HYPOTHETICAL), a former Permanent Forces corporal, discharged with an accepted knee condition.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 78(5), (6) -- the lump sum`

-- The arguments: weekly amount in the notice; s 74 maximum; percentage chosen; factor for the age; factor for a male of
-- 30; weekly amounts paid since the notice date.
-- $100 a week is 23.7% of $421.72, so 25, 50, 75 or 100% may be converted. 50%: 0.5 × 100 × 900 = 45,000, less 50% of
-- the $400 paid since the notice date (200): 44,800.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 100 421.72 50 900 1000 400 EQUALS JUST 44800
-- A member under 30, whose factor (1,100) is above a 30-year-old man's: capped at 0.5 × 100 × 1,000 = 50,000; less 200: 49,800.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 100 421.72 50 1100 1000 400 EQUALS JUST 49800
-- $50 a week is 11.9% of the maximum: only 50% or 100% (s 78(1)(b)); 75% is not open, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 50 421.72 75 900 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same at 50%: 0.5 × 50 × 900 = 22,500.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 50 421.72 50 900 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 22500
-- $30 a week is 7.1% of the maximum: only 100% (s 78(1)(a)): 30 × 900 = 27,000; 50% is not open.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 30 421.72 100 900 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 27000
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum` 30 421.72 50 900 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The arguments: service; impairment points; lifestyle rating; s 74 maximum; percentage; the two factors; amounts paid.
-- On the Guide's amount: non-warlike service, 15 points, lifestyle 1: factor 0.155 (Table 23.1), 0.155 × 421.72 = 65.3666
-- a week, 15.5% of the maximum, so 50% may be converted: 0.5 × 65.3666 × 900 = 29,414.97.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum on the Guide's amount` `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping` 15 1 421.72 50 900 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 29414.97
-- 3 points: below the Guide's table (it starts at 5), no weekly amount, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum on the Guide's amount` `peacetime service` 3 1 421.72 100 900 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 141, 179 -- normal earnings`

-- The arguments: ADF pay; allowance component; the $100 in force; national minimum wage per hour.
-- Sam: ADF pay $1,500, allowances $200: 1,500 + 200 + 100 = 1,800, above 24.95 × 38 = 948.10.
#ASSERT `my normal earnings as a former Permanent Forces member` 1500 200 100 24.95 EQUALS 1800
-- A recruit on $700, no allowances: 700 + 0 + 100 = 800, below 948.10, raised to it (s 179).
#ASSERT `my normal earnings as a former Permanent Forces member` 700 0 100 24.95 EQUALS 948.1

§§ `ss 129 to 131 -- weekly incapacity compensation`

-- The arguments: kept from work by an accepted condition; Special Rate Disability Pension; normal weekly hours; hours lost
-- before this week; hours lost this week; hours worked; pension age; within 2 years of it; weeks compensated; in prison;
-- normal earnings; able to earn in suitable work; earned this week. 37.5 hours: the 45-week total is 1,687.5.
-- Week 10, off entirely: 375 hours, a maximum rate week: 1,800 − 0 = 1,800 (s 129).
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 337.5 37.5 0 FALSE FALSE 9 FALSE 1800 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1800
-- Week 10, working half his hours for $600 (and able to earn that): 1,800 − 600 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 337.5 18.75 18.75 FALSE FALSE 9 FALSE 1800 600 600 EQUALS JUST 1200
-- Past the 1,687.5 hours, not working: 75% × 1,800 = 1,350 (s 131).
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 2000 37.5 0 FALSE FALSE 55 FALSE 1800 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1350
-- Past them, working 18.75 of 37.5 hours (50%, so 85%) for $700: 0.85 × 1,800 = 1,530; 1,530 − 700 = 830.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 2000 18.75 18.75 FALSE FALSE 55 FALSE 1800 700 700 EQUALS JUST 830
-- The week that crosses the line (s 130), off entirely: 1,668.75 before, so 18.75 maximum rate hours, 18.75 reduced rate
-- hours: (18.75/37.5) × 1,800 = 900, plus (18.75/37.5) × 1,350 = 675: 1,575.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 1668.75 37.5 0 FALSE FALSE 44 FALSE 1800 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1575
-- Able to earn $2,000 in suitable work, more than normal earnings: negative, read as nil.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 337.5 37.5 0 FALSE FALSE 9 FALSE 1800 2000 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Has chosen the Special Rate Disability Pension: Part 6, not encoded, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE TRUE 37.5 337.5 37.5 0 FALSE FALSE 9 FALSE 1800 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- At pension age, the condition not within 2 years before it (s 120): nil.
#ASSERT `How much incapacity compensation this week` TRUE FALSE 37.5 2000 37.5 0 TRUE FALSE 55 FALSE 1800 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `s 404 -- indexation`

-- The arguments: December index number for the previous financial year; highest earlier December index number.
-- 142.0 / 138.0 = 1.028985...: 3 places 1.028, 4th place 9, more than 4: 1.029.
#ASSERT `the s 404 indexation factor to 3 places` 142 138 EQUALS 1.029
-- The arguments: amount for the previous financial year; December CPI; highest earlier December CPI; the s 74(1) amount;
-- brought-forward amount left.
-- The s 74(1) maximum of $421.72, nothing brought forward left: 421.72 × 1.029 = 433.94988.
#ASSERT `the MRCA amount for the indexation year` 421.72 142 138 TRUE 0 EQUALS 433.94988
-- With the whole 0.007 still brought forward: 1.029 − 0.007 = 1.022; 421.72 × 1.022 = 430.99784.
#ASSERT `the MRCA amount for the indexation year` 421.72 142 138 TRUE 0.007 EQUALS 430.99784
-- The same factor on another amount (not s 74(1)): the brought-forward amount does not apply, 433.94988.
#ASSERT `the MRCA amount for the indexation year` 421.72 142 138 FALSE 0.007 EQUALS 433.94988
-- A factor of 1.005 on s 74(1) less 0.007 would be 0.998: not below 1 (s 404(5A)), so the amount stays 421.72.
#ASSERT `the MRCA amount for the indexation year` 421.72 100.5 100 TRUE 0.007 EQUALS 421.72
-- The December CPI below the highest earlier one: factor under 1, no replacement.
#ASSERT `the MRCA amount for the indexation year` 421.72 137 138 FALSE 0 EQUALS 421.72
